{% extends "base.html" %}
{% block title %}Support and learning{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h1>Support and learning</h1>
<p class="notice"><strong>If you are in immediate danger, contact your local emergency services.</strong> LESEDI does not replace emergency services, qualified legal advice, medical care or professional counselling.</p>
<p>This section is a placeholder for content that qualified people have reviewed. It deliberately contains no hotline numbers or organisation details: those must be added through a reviewed process with source, review date and reviewer, and must never be guessed.</p>
<h2>Planned sections (not yet written)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Recognise</strong>: warning signs of abuse, coercion, stalking and digital abuse.</li>
  <li><strong>Safety planning</strong>: preparation checklists.</li>
  <li><strong>Leave</strong>: careful preparation. Leaving is not always the safest choice.</li>
  <li><strong>Speak</strong>: options for getting support. You are never forced to report.</li>
  <li><strong>Heal</strong>: emotional, social and legal support.</li>
</ul>
<p class="help">Languages: this build is English only. A translation framework and South African Sign Language content are not built yet.</p>
{% endblock %}
